@startuml
title HPC Dask Evaluation Sequence (remote scheduler)

actor Driver as User
participant "Trainer\n(EATrainer/CMAESTrainer/PSOTrainer)" as T
participant "make_executor\n(utils.parallel)" as ME
participant "_DaskExecutor" as DE
database "Registry" as R
participant "dask.distributed.Client" as C
participant "Remote Scheduler" as S
participant "Remote Worker(s)" as WK

== Resolve connection ==
User -> T: train(config)
T -> ME: make_executor(num_workers, backend="dask",\n  dask_client=None, scheduler_address=config.scheduler_address)
ME -> ME: resolve_scheduler_address(arg)\n  precedence: arg > DEAP_DASK_SCHEDULER env var
note right: no client/address/env var\n-> falls back to an auto-built\nlocal LocalCluster (unchanged\nsingle-machine default)
ME -> DE: _DaskExecutor(scheduler_address=effective_address)
DE -> C: Client(address=...) or Client(scheduler_file=...)
C -> S: connect
S --> C: connected
DE -> C: client.wait_for_workers(1, timeout=DEAP_DASK_CONNECT_TIMEOUT)
C -> S: poll worker registrations
S --> C: worker(s) joined
DE -> C: client.forward_logging()
note right: worker-side logging records\nnow surface on the driver

== Post-connect checks (warn-only) ==
DE -> C: client.scheduler_info()
C --> DE: worker nthreads, addresses
DE -> DE: warn if any worker nthreads > 1
DE -> C: client.run(importlib.metadata.version, "deap-pettingzoo")
C -> WK: run on every worker
WK --> C: installed version per worker
DE -> DE: warn on driver/worker version mismatch
DE --> ME: executor (worker_info() available)
ME --> T: executor

== Dispatch population ==
T -> R: get_registry_snapshot(target_remote=True)
R --> T: snapshot (custom envs; warns + drops\nnon-picklable / __main__ factories)
T -> T: build _EvalWorkerSpec(..., registry_snapshot)
T -> DE: executor.map(_worker_evaluate, payloads, retries=2)
alt worker fn resolves to __main__
  DE -> DE: raise immediately\n(fn.__module__ == "__main__")
else fn resolvable
  DE -> C: client.map(_worker_evaluate, payloads, retries=2)
  C -> WK: dispatch payload
  WK -> WK: replay_registry_snapshot_once(snapshot)
  WK -> WK: rebuild env/policy/evaluator\n(per-process worker cache)
  WK -> WK: run episode(s) -> (fitness, steps_delta)
  WK --> C: result
  note right: idempotent retry on worker death\n(evaluations are pure); deterministic\nfailures surface after 3 attempts with\nthe real remote traceback via client.gather
  C --> DE: ordered results (map preserves\ninput/output order)
end
DE --> T: fitness list + step_sink accumulation

== Result ==
T -> T: record metadata: num_workers, parallel_backend,\n  scheduler_address, dask_workers (observed hosts)
T --> User: TrainingResult(policy, metrics, metadata)
@enduml
